Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Harmoniq project.

## Changes Made:

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package (v1.4.1) using npm
- Updated package.json with the new dependency
- Updated package-lock.json with dependency tree

### 2. Analytics Configuration
Modified `/frontend/src/app/layout.tsx`:
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the `<body>` element, after the QueryProvider component

## Implementation Details:

The Analytics component was added following the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router projects (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart). The component was placed:
- After all other content in the body
- Inside the ClerkProvider context
- As a sibling to the QueryProvider component

This placement ensures:
1. Analytics tracking works across all routes
2. The component doesn't interfere with existing functionality
3. The tracking script is loaded after the main content

## Verification:

✅ TypeScript compilation: No errors
✅ Build process: Completed successfully
✅ Linter: No new errors (3 pre-existing warnings unrelated to this change)
✅ Test suite: All 109 tests passed across 16 test files
✅ Package manager: npm lock file properly updated

## Next Steps:

To enable analytics data collection:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard under Analytics settings
3. Analytics data will be available in the Vercel dashboard after deployment

The implementation is complete and ready for deployment.
